    "details": "Trifecta Tech Foundation reports:\n\n> Users that are explicitly permitted to edit only specific files using\n> sudoedit, are still able to place files in arbitrary directories.\n>\n> This only affects systems where sudoedit is used to give very\n> fine-grained edit permissions, which is not the default configuration.\n> For users that have full sudoedit permission or no sudoedit permission\n> at all, no escalation is enabled by this bug.\n>\n> A user that is allowed to place files in an arbitrary directory can\n> (by placing a file in /etc/sudoers.d) obviously fully escalate their\n> privileges.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0429",
    "modified": "2026-08-31T00:00:00Z",
    "published": "2026-08-31T00:00:00Z",
